WEBVTT

00:00:14.917 --> 00:00:19.750
I'm your big brother.
If I don't teach you this, who will?

00:00:22.583 --> 00:00:26.958
I don't know, Trey.
- Quit being a little bitch. Get in.

00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:29.083
Yeah. Let's go.

00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:32.125
Get in.

00:00:32.542 --> 00:00:34.917
Come on, let's go, Ryan.

00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:50.042
You know, you should see your face, man.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.250
No. No.

00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:12.708
Let me see those hands. Let's go.

00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:18.458
Hands up. Get them up. On the dash,
where I can see them. Let's go.

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:35.708
Ryan. Sandy Cohen.

00:01:35.875 --> 00:01:39.667
The court's appointed me
your public defender.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.167
You could do worse. You okay?
They treating you all right?

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.500
Where's my brother?

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:50.583
Trey is over 18. Trey stole a car.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.250
Trey had a gun in his pants, an ounce
of pot in his jacket, a couple of priors.

00:01:54.333 --> 00:01:57.292
I'm guessing right now
Trey is looking at three to five years.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:59.083
But Trey's not my concern.

00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:00.917
This is your first time in lockup.

00:02:01.042 --> 00:02:03.458
I'm assuming you don't plan
on coming back.

00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:06.333
Your grades are not great.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.667
Suspended twice for fighting,
truancy three times.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:17.417
Your test scores.
Ninety-eighth percentile on your SAT I's.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.667
Ryan, 98th percentile.
If you start going to class...

00:02:20.792 --> 00:02:23.458
Are you thinking about college?

00:02:23.625 --> 00:02:26.417
Have you given any thought at all
to your future?

00:02:26.542 --> 00:02:30.042
Dude, I'm on your side.

00:02:30.208 --> 00:02:31.708
Help me out here, give...

00:02:31.792 --> 00:02:37.375
Modern medicine is advancing to the point
where the average life span will be 100.

00:02:37.458 --> 00:02:43.000
But I read this article which said Social
Security is supposed to run out by 2025...

00:02:43.083 --> 00:02:49.417
...which means people are gonna
have to stay in their jobs until they're 80.

00:02:50.875 --> 00:02:54.792
So I don't want to commit
to anything too soon.

00:02:55.792 --> 00:02:59.542
Look, I can plea this down
to a misdemeanor. Petty fine, probation.

00:02:59.625 --> 00:03:02.375
But stealing a car because
your big brother told you to...

00:03:02.458 --> 00:03:03.917
...it's stupid and it's weak.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.125
Those are two things
you can't afford to be anymore.

00:03:06.208 --> 00:03:08.042
Two more things.
- Want to change that?

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:11.042
Then get over the fact
that life dealt you a bad hand.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:13.875
I get it. We're cut
from the same deck, Ryan.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.542
I grew up with no money, my father
was gone, my mother worked all the time.

00:03:18.625 --> 00:03:21.042
I was pissed off, I was stupid.

00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:23.125
Look at you now.

00:03:25.708 --> 00:03:30.500
Smart kid like you, you gotta
have a plan, some kind of a dream.

00:03:30.625 --> 00:03:32.583
Yeah. Right.

00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:34.708
Let me tell you something, okay?

00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:38.542
Where I'm from, having a dream
doesn't make you smart.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:41.000
Knowing it won't come true?

00:03:41.458 --> 00:03:43.458
That does.

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:47.875
My office will contact you
to remind you of your hearing date.

00:03:47.958 --> 00:03:49.958
I'll remember.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:06.208
Unbelievable.
What kind of family I got, huh?

00:04:06.292 --> 00:04:10.458
What the hell did I do to deserve
this family? You want to tell me that?

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.833
Mrs. Atwood? I'm Sandy Cohen.
I'm Ryan's attorney.

00:04:13.958 --> 00:04:16.167
You should have let him rot in there.

00:04:16.292 --> 00:04:20.958
Just like his dad's doing,
and just like his brother's gonna.

00:04:21.042 --> 00:04:23.125
Let's go, Ryan.

00:04:23.917 --> 00:04:25.917
Now, Ryan.

00:04:26.542 --> 00:04:30.042
I'm gonna give you my card
and my home number.

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:34.125
You know, if you need somebody,
if things get to be too much...

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.625
...call me.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.167
Let's go.
- All right.

00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:44.292
I can't do this anymore, Ryan.

00:04:44.458 --> 00:04:46.458
I can't.

00:04:46.625 --> 00:04:50.375
I'm sorry, Mom.
- I want you out of my house.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:56.167
I want you out.
- But, Mom, where am I gonna go?

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:59.708
You heard your mother, man. Get out.
- This isn't your house, man.

00:04:59.833 --> 00:05:03.500
Oh, you a tough guy now?
- A.J., don't. Ryan, just get out.

00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:09.542
You should worry about your own kids
instead of freeloading off my mom.

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:29.542
Hey. Can I crash with you tonight?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.375
Yeah, all right. Fine.

00:05:33.917 --> 00:05:39.958
I need a place to crash tonight.
I already tried it. I already tried it.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.917
I told you. You could do worse.

00:07:01.792 --> 00:07:04.917
This is a nice car. I didn't know
your kind of lawyer made money.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.583
No, we don't.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:09.750
My wife does.

00:07:13.375 --> 00:07:15.958
Good evening, Mr. Cohen.

00:07:26.125 --> 00:07:31.208
You know, why don't you
wait here for a minute. I'll be back.

00:07:31.708 --> 00:07:34.750
It's no fun if the key's in the car.

00:07:36.167 --> 00:07:39.583
T- shirt and bumper stickers
from the radio station.

00:07:39.667 --> 00:07:41.917
You brought him home?

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:46.208
This is not a stray puppy, Sandy.
- I know that, Kirsten.

00:07:46.333 --> 00:07:50.250
It was only a matter of time before
you started bringing home felons.

00:07:50.375 --> 00:07:53.500
Ryan's not a felon.
- Did you not meet him in jail?

00:07:53.583 --> 00:07:56.625
Yes, technically.
But it wasn't for a felony.

00:07:56.708 --> 00:07:59.042
It was, but it won't be when I'm done.

00:07:59.125 --> 00:08:02.667
You're endangering our home.
Did you even think of Seth?

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.833
It's only for the weekend.
Till Child Services opens on Monday.

00:08:05.958 --> 00:08:09.667
What if this is all a scam?
What if he's using you to case the house?

00:08:09.792 --> 00:08:11.792
He's not a criminal mastermind.

00:08:11.917 --> 00:08:14.458
He's a kid who has no one,
and nowhere to go.

00:08:14.542 --> 00:08:18.542
When did you become so cynical?
- When did you become so self-righteous?

00:08:18.625 --> 00:08:21.292
I've always been self-righteous.

00:08:21.625 --> 00:08:25.250
You used to find it charming.
- He sleeps in the pool house.

00:08:25.333 --> 00:08:29.500
Where you going?
- To put my jewelry in the vault.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.958
Where do you think I'm going?

00:08:33.458 --> 00:08:35.917
The boy's gonna need fresh sheets...

00:08:36.042 --> 00:08:39.042
...and towels and a toothbrush.

00:08:55.667 --> 00:08:59.042
Who are you?
- Whoever you want me to be.

00:09:00.875 --> 00:09:02.875
Okay.

00:09:11.042 --> 00:09:13.333
Hey, can I bum a cigarette?

00:09:44.792 --> 00:09:47.542
So, what are you doing here? Seriously.

00:09:47.625 --> 00:09:49.625
Seriously?

00:09:55.083 --> 00:09:57.167
I stole a car.

00:09:58.458 --> 00:10:00.875
Crashed it.

00:10:01.833 --> 00:10:04.292
Actually, my brother did.

00:10:04.458 --> 00:10:08.083
Since he had a gun and drugs on him,
he's in jail.

00:10:08.208 --> 00:10:14.000
I got out, then my mom threw me out.
She was pissed off and drunk.

00:10:15.125 --> 00:10:17.167
So Mr. Cohen took me in.

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:23.583
You're their cousin from Boston, right?

00:10:23.875 --> 00:10:25.458
Right.

00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:28.292
Hi, Marissa.
- Hey, Mr. Cohen.

00:10:28.458 --> 00:10:31.083
I was just meeting your nephew.

00:10:32.833 --> 00:10:35.167
My favorite nephew, Ryan.

00:10:35.333 --> 00:10:37.542
All the way from Seattle.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:41.958
Seattle.
- Dad lives there. Mom lives in Boston.

00:10:42.042 --> 00:10:45.542
So we're all really excited about your
fashion show fundraiser tomorrow.

00:10:45.625 --> 00:10:47.667
Really? You are?

00:10:49.333 --> 00:10:51.333
No.

00:10:55.542 --> 00:10:57.542
Come on, let's go.

00:10:57.875 --> 00:11:01.958
Hey, you should come by, check it out.
If you don't have other plans.

00:11:02.042 --> 00:11:04.042
See you.
- Good night.

00:11:10.958 --> 00:11:12.958
Who's that kid?

00:11:14.958 --> 00:11:17.042
Let's go inside.

00:11:21.458 --> 00:11:24.250
There's no smoking in this house.

00:11:33.167 --> 00:11:35.292
So this is where you'll be staying.

00:11:35.375 --> 00:11:38.250
And this is the queen
of the manor herself, my wife, Kirsten.

00:11:38.333 --> 00:11:41.458
Hello, Ryan. Welcome to our home.

00:11:41.625 --> 00:11:45.417
If you need anything,
Rosie here can help you.

00:11:47.208 --> 00:11:49.667
Thank you. Thanks very much.

00:11:52.125 --> 00:11:56.792
We'll see you in the morning.
Make yourself comfortable.

00:12:36.125 --> 00:12:38.125
Hey.

00:12:38.417 --> 00:12:40.417
Hey.

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:45.250
Do you wanna play?

00:12:46.333 --> 00:12:52.042
Looks like someone's trying to be
a hero, but he got a little cocky.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.750
What happened to your head, dude?
Where did it go?

00:12:56.833 --> 00:12:58.250
I'm sorry. Did someone die?

00:12:58.333 --> 00:13:03.500
Hey, want to play 'Grand Theft Auto'?
It's pretty cool. You can steal cars and...

00:13:03.583 --> 00:13:05.583
Not that that's cool.

00:13:05.625 --> 00:13:08.708
Or uncool, I don't know...
- I see you two have met.

00:13:08.792 --> 00:13:11.000
Seth, what are you doing inside
on this beautiful day?

00:13:11.125 --> 00:13:14.208
Why don't you show Ryan around?
- Because it's so great around here.

00:13:14.333 --> 00:13:15.667
There's so much to do, Dad.

00:13:15.792 --> 00:13:18.208
I don't know,
what do you want to do?

00:13:18.333 --> 00:13:21.042
What do you guys do around here?

00:13:41.667 --> 00:13:46.958
I have this plan.
I don't know what you'll think.

00:13:47.125 --> 00:13:50.708
But next July the trade winds shift west,
and I want to sail to Tahiti.

00:13:50.792 --> 00:13:54.083
I could do it in 44 days,
maybe even 42.

00:13:54.125 --> 00:13:55.792
Wow, that...

00:13:55.875 --> 00:13:59.167
That sounds really cool, man.
- Yeah.

00:13:59.667 --> 00:14:01.375
You just hit the high seas...

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:05.875
...and catch fish off the side of the boat,
grill them right there.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.000
Just total quiet.

00:14:08.667 --> 00:14:10.667
Solitude.

00:14:11.958 --> 00:14:15.750
You won't get Ionely?
- Well, I'll have Summer with me.

00:14:15.833 --> 00:14:18.667
You're gonna take this to Tahiti?

00:14:23.458 --> 00:14:25.125
No.

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:28.083
It's the girl the boat's named after.

00:14:28.208 --> 00:14:30.417
She must be pretty stoked.

00:14:30.583 --> 00:14:35.250
Yeah. She has no idea.
I've never talked to her before.

00:14:40.792 --> 00:14:42.583
Hey, fellas.

00:14:42.667 --> 00:14:44.958
I thought we'd head over
to the fashion show at 7.

00:14:45.083 --> 00:14:46.583
Yeah. Have fun.

00:14:46.708 --> 00:14:51.417
Come on. It's a whole new school year.
- It's also the same kids, Dad.

00:14:51.542 --> 00:14:54.875
Why do they need a fashion show?
Every day is a fashion show for them.

00:14:54.958 --> 00:14:58.000
Ryan has to go. Marissa invited him.

00:14:58.875 --> 00:15:01.458
Marissa invited you?

00:15:01.625 --> 00:15:04.792
I've lived next door
to Marissa since, like, forever.

00:15:04.875 --> 00:15:07.000
Her dad almost got married to my mom.

00:15:07.125 --> 00:15:09.625
And she's never even invited me
to a birthday.

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:13.625
That is not true.
They did not almost get married.

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:16.083
Maybe Summer would be there.

00:15:16.167 --> 00:15:20.250
That's interesting.
She is Marissa's best friend.

00:15:20.625 --> 00:15:22.792
Seven?
- Seven.

00:15:47.125 --> 00:15:50.417
Hello again.
- My dad's not here.

00:15:50.583 --> 00:15:53.833
When can we expect him?
- I don't know.

00:15:55.625 --> 00:15:57.458
Well, when you see your father...

00:15:57.583 --> 00:16:01.500
...please remind him again
how much we'd like to talk.

00:16:01.625 --> 00:16:05.083
Let me leave you another one of my cards.

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.250
Have a good day.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.500
Hey.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:27.958
Thanks, kiddo. I just didn't have time
to deal with those guys right now.

00:16:28.042 --> 00:16:30.042
Who are they?

00:16:31.458 --> 00:16:33.208
Suits.

00:16:33.292 --> 00:16:35.375
Bureaucrats.

00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:38.042
The Man.

00:16:39.917 --> 00:16:41.875
But, I mean, everything's okay, right?

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:46.167
Yeah. It's just a...
Just a thing with a client.

00:16:47.125 --> 00:16:50.250
Nothing for you to worry about, okay?

00:17:17.833 --> 00:17:21.500
Wow, look at that.
It fits you beautifully.

00:17:21.667 --> 00:17:23.500
Where's your tie?

00:17:23.583 --> 00:17:27.333
I'm not gonna wear one.
Open collar, it's a good look.

00:17:27.417 --> 00:17:33.458
I didn't know how to tie a tie till
I was 25. Come on, give me your tie.

00:17:34.542 --> 00:17:36.667
Button your top button.

00:17:39.292 --> 00:17:40.917
All right. Collar up.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:45.125
The skinny side has got to be shorter
than the fat side.

00:17:45.208 --> 00:17:48.167
How much shorter,
it changes tie to tie.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:51.083
Sometimes it's just a mystery.

00:17:51.875 --> 00:17:53.833
All right.

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:56.958
So you got to hang out with Seth.

00:17:57.042 --> 00:17:58.542
How was that? Was that...?

00:17:58.625 --> 00:18:00.917
Was that all right?

00:18:01.333 --> 00:18:03.583
He's an interesting kid
if you get to know him.

00:18:03.667 --> 00:18:05.667
He's cool.

00:18:07.583 --> 00:18:09.583
Cool, huh?

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:13.750
All right.

00:18:14.333 --> 00:18:17.458
There we go. Turn around.

00:18:17.625 --> 00:18:19.625
Look at you.

00:18:24.292 --> 00:18:26.292
Beats a jumpsuit.

00:18:38.875 --> 00:18:40.917
Oh, Mom, do you like my nails?

00:18:41.042 --> 00:18:46.583
I love them, Kaitlin. Do you like my hair
this straight, or is it too Avril Lavigne?

00:18:46.667 --> 00:18:48.542
No, it looks good, Mom.

00:18:48.625 --> 00:18:50.667
Marissa, you look...

00:18:50.833 --> 00:18:53.708
Oh, honey, I thought
you were gonna wear your hair down.

00:18:53.792 --> 00:18:56.458
Pulled back like that,
it's harsh on your angles.

00:18:56.583 --> 00:18:58.542
Okay. Let's go.

00:18:58.625 --> 00:19:00.208
It's gonna be so amazing tonight.

00:19:00.333 --> 00:19:03.292
Are you gonna wear the Donna Karan,
Mariss? It's very forgiving.

00:19:03.417 --> 00:19:05.625
You look beautiful, kiddo.

00:19:13.708 --> 00:19:17.708
Mushroom-leek crescent?
Crab-and-brie filo?

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:23.167
Welcome to the dark side.

00:19:27.875 --> 00:19:30.458
So you must be the cousin from Boston.

00:19:30.542 --> 00:19:36.000
I don't know how you do it. I could
just never live there. I hate the cold.

00:19:36.083 --> 00:19:41.250
Do you like Seattle? I mean,
all that rain. Isn't it depressing?

00:19:41.333 --> 00:19:44.208
Did I hear you were from Canada?

00:19:45.083 --> 00:19:47.208
Yes, you did.

00:19:53.417 --> 00:19:57.333
Hi. Can I get a 7 and 7?
- Sure.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.750
Thanks.

00:20:15.167 --> 00:20:17.167
Thank you.

00:20:18.917 --> 00:20:22.417
I want my husband to be right about you.

00:20:28.667 --> 00:20:33.000
What's up? Lock it up, Nordlund.
- Lock it up, Luke.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.500
Hey, Luke. What's up?

00:20:37.667 --> 00:20:40.000
Hey.
- Hey.

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.000
Suck it, queer.

00:20:45.083 --> 00:20:49.792
My vacation was great too.
Thank you for asking about it.

00:20:52.958 --> 00:20:55.000
Summer's right over there. Don't look.

00:20:55.125 --> 00:20:59.167
You can look,
but don't look like you're looking.

00:20:59.417 --> 00:21:01.208
Hey, Dad.
- Hey, guys.

00:21:01.292 --> 00:21:03.417
Who is that?

00:21:03.583 --> 00:21:07.458
The cousin? The pool boy?
I don't know.

00:21:07.625 --> 00:21:10.083
Well, I'm gonna find out.

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:12.250
Is that Summer?

00:21:12.333 --> 00:21:15.042
I'm gonna... I'm gonna sit.

00:21:17.333 --> 00:21:20.042
Way to salt his game, Mr. Cohen.

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:26.458
Hello, Chester. Are these seats taken?

00:21:29.083 --> 00:21:31.042
Okay.

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:46.042
So are you looking forward to your next
sailing lesson? You're making strides.

00:21:46.167 --> 00:21:50.583
Okay. I'm glad we had
this little chance to catch up.

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:53.417
Thank you. Thank you.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:57.042
Thank you all so much for coming.

00:21:57.125 --> 00:22:00.917
Every year we do this to raise money
for the battered women's shelter.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.208
It's such a good cause, you guys.

00:22:03.333 --> 00:22:05.583
We couldn't do any of it
without your support...

00:22:05.708 --> 00:22:08.917
...and the support of Fashion Island
and all their great stores.

00:22:09.042 --> 00:22:11.708
All right, enjoy the show.

00:22:25.542 --> 00:22:28.750
She's got Tahiti written all over her.

00:22:34.208 --> 00:22:37.625
Has anybody seen
my Betsey Johnson dress?

00:22:39.708 --> 00:22:44.208
All right. Oh, no.
Much too much makeup. Let's go.

00:22:44.375 --> 00:22:47.167
What are you doing
putting my daughter in Calvin Klein?

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:48.958
She was supposed to wear Vera Wang.

00:22:49.042 --> 00:22:53.292
She would if she had the chest to hold
it up. It's called puberty. It'll happen.

00:22:53.417 --> 00:22:56.167
Okay, girls, chop-chop, showtime.

00:23:02.375 --> 00:23:04.375
Marissa, you're next.

00:23:09.667 --> 00:23:11.667
Look what I stole.

00:23:11.708 --> 00:23:13.708
Look what I stole.

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:17.292
All right. Here.
- Thanks.

00:23:45.167 --> 00:23:47.625
She's so beautiful, you guys.

00:23:47.667 --> 00:23:50.583
You spent more on that dress
than I make in a year.

00:23:50.667 --> 00:23:55.042
That's why we trust him with our money.
I expect to die a very rich man.

00:23:55.125 --> 00:23:57.667
You're bound to be half-right.

00:23:59.458 --> 00:24:00.875
You okay, Jimmy?

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:05.625
Yeah. It's just...
It's a little stuffy in here.

00:24:05.792 --> 00:24:08.708
Honey, I'm gonna get some fresh air, okay?

00:24:08.792 --> 00:24:11.333
Marissa wanted to wear
these Prada Mary Janes...

00:24:11.417 --> 00:24:16.000
...but I told her she had to wear
the stiletto Manolos.

00:24:59.583 --> 00:25:01.708
Hey, where are you going?

00:25:03.083 --> 00:25:07.417
My friend Holly... Well, her parents are
letting us use their beach house...

00:25:07.500 --> 00:25:11.292
...as a gift because of all our hard work
for charity.

00:25:11.417 --> 00:25:14.125
If you need a ride...

00:25:14.292 --> 00:25:17.083
...or anything...

00:25:17.250 --> 00:25:19.250
...I'm Summer.

00:25:28.333 --> 00:25:29.917
Hey, you ready to go?
- Yeah.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.917
We should go to that party
at that girl Holly's place.

00:25:33.042 --> 00:25:36.375
No, that's not really for us.
- Summer invited me.

00:25:36.500 --> 00:25:38.708
Really? She did?

00:25:39.750 --> 00:25:43.000
Us. She...
She asked for you, actually.

00:25:43.750 --> 00:25:46.000
Really? She did?

00:25:48.167 --> 00:25:50.167
Come on.

00:25:52.125 --> 00:25:55.667
That makes absolutely no sense,
but, yes, we should go.

00:25:55.792 --> 00:25:59.000
We're gonna go with them.
Thanks, guys.

00:26:10.750 --> 00:26:13.458
If it sucks, we can always bail.

00:26:47.458 --> 00:26:49.708
Welcome to the dark side.

00:26:52.542 --> 00:26:55.542
Oh, hey, cocaine. That's awesome.

00:27:00.750 --> 00:27:03.667
Is that a new purse?
- Yeah.

00:27:03.792 --> 00:27:06.875
So cute.
- Does your dad ever say no?

00:27:10.750 --> 00:27:13.917
Hey. Look who I brought.

00:27:16.708 --> 00:27:18.875
He's cute.

00:27:20.542 --> 00:27:23.417
I'm gonna play him hot and cold.

00:27:26.750 --> 00:27:29.333
You wanna pee? I've gotta pee.

00:27:39.167 --> 00:27:43.583
Isn't it, like, so beautiful?
The sand and the water.

00:27:43.583 --> 00:27:46.875
Yeah. Hey, you want to go check it out?

00:27:47.542 --> 00:27:49.583
But what about Marissa?

00:27:49.750 --> 00:27:52.042
Oh, no worries.

00:28:16.625 --> 00:28:18.833
Hey, Jimmy.
- Hey.

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:20.750
Hey, Dustin.

00:28:20.875 --> 00:28:22.917
Dustin, look who's here.

00:28:25.792 --> 00:28:29.875
Are you really okay?
- Oh, yeah, yeah. Yeah.

00:28:30.042 --> 00:28:34.333
Because you can always...
- I've just been working really hard.

00:28:34.417 --> 00:28:37.333
So who was that kid
that you brought tonight?

00:28:37.417 --> 00:28:40.167
You have a cousin from Boston?

00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:46.000
One of Sandy's clients.
He brought him home for the weekend.

00:28:48.125 --> 00:28:51.500
Jimmy? Honey, did you get my fro-yo?

00:28:52.292 --> 00:28:54.333
No. I forgot.

00:28:56.042 --> 00:28:58.167
All right, I'll go back.

00:28:58.625 --> 00:29:02.042
Pistachio. Thanks, sweetie. Hi, Kirsten.

00:29:09.500 --> 00:29:11.500
Fro-yo.

00:29:12.292 --> 00:29:15.958
Did you ever think this would be our lives?

00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:19.750
Is Marissa back yet?
- Well, she usually stays out pretty late.

00:29:19.833 --> 00:29:22.042
Well, Seth never goes out.

00:29:22.583 --> 00:29:24.583
Don't worry.

00:29:24.958 --> 00:29:29.042
I'm sure they're not
doing anything we didn't do.

00:29:29.500 --> 00:29:31.500
That's comforting.

00:29:39.625 --> 00:29:43.125
I'm sorry. I should really learn to knock...

00:29:43.208 --> 00:29:47.875
...in case there's a threesome
going on in the bathroom.

00:29:55.833 --> 00:29:59.333
Fresh keg. Everybody get naked.

00:30:07.292 --> 00:30:09.250
Hey.

00:30:09.958 --> 00:30:13.250
Hey.
- So, what do you think of Newport?

00:30:15.042 --> 00:30:19.125
I think I can get in less trouble
where I'm from.

00:30:21.708 --> 00:30:24.875
Hey, Coop, it's your turn to deal.

00:30:28.125 --> 00:30:30.375
You have no idea.

00:30:34.042 --> 00:30:37.500
I fixed the keg. Fine, more for me.

00:30:49.167 --> 00:30:52.417
Look who I found.

00:30:55.083 --> 00:30:57.083
I'm wasted.

00:30:57.292 --> 00:31:00.292
So, what's your name anyway?
- Ryan.

00:31:00.458 --> 00:31:02.958
Ryan.

00:31:06.292 --> 00:31:09.250
What are you doing?
- Excuse me.

00:31:10.458 --> 00:31:12.917
What are you doing?
I named my boat after her.

00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:15.875
What? Who are you?

00:31:16.042 --> 00:31:18.083
It's not what you think.
She's drunk.

00:31:18.208 --> 00:31:20.208
Come on.

00:31:22.292 --> 00:31:25.000
Seth, Seth.
- Don't touch me.

00:31:25.167 --> 00:31:27.542
You know what,
why don't you just go back to Chino?

00:31:27.625 --> 00:31:33.917
I'm sure there's a really nice car
in the parking lot that you could steal.

00:31:36.375 --> 00:31:38.375
Chino?

00:32:07.000 --> 00:32:10.583
Go home, geek.
- Who invited you, suck-ass?

00:32:15.125 --> 00:32:18.875
You guys really wouldn't hurt me,
because that would be so clich��d.

00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:21.375
I guess you're fans of the clich��.
- Shut up.

00:32:21.500 --> 00:32:25.000
Hey, put him down. Put him down.

00:32:25.167 --> 00:32:27.917
Hey, Ryan. What's up?

00:32:28.250 --> 00:32:29.583
Put him down.

00:32:29.667 --> 00:32:32.958
Hey, what's up, dude?
You got a problem?

00:32:35.042 --> 00:32:37.000
You tell me.

00:33:01.958 --> 00:33:04.500
Welcome to the O.C., bitch.

00:33:04.667 --> 00:33:07.958
This is how it's done in Orange County.

00:33:38.083 --> 00:33:40.083
Well...

00:33:40.458 --> 00:33:43.000
...I don't know what to say...

00:33:43.750 --> 00:33:47.833
...except that you totally
had my back out there.

00:33:49.417 --> 00:33:52.333
You were, like, out of Fight Club
or something. I don't know.

00:33:52.458 --> 00:33:54.458
You know what I think?

00:33:54.625 --> 00:33:57.708
Ryan, I think that if you were
to teach me some moves...

00:33:57.833 --> 00:34:01.125
...I think that we could
totally take them next time.

00:34:01.208 --> 00:34:04.917
A little bit of that, you know what
I mean? And a little bit of that, that.

00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:08.458
What do you think about that? Yeah.

00:34:08.625 --> 00:34:14.542
Oh, also, that wasn't exactly the way
that I first planned to talk to Summer...

00:34:14.667 --> 00:34:17.333
...but I'm now on her radar.

00:34:17.500 --> 00:34:21.333
Do you think I should tell her
about Tahiti? Do you?

00:34:21.458 --> 00:34:23.542
Not yet.
- That's what I thought.

00:34:23.625 --> 00:34:28.958
That's what I was thinking. I wanted
to make sure we were on the same page.

00:34:29.042 --> 00:34:31.833
What a little night we had there.

00:34:33.125 --> 00:34:38.250
I'm not gonna forget it.
Ryan, I'm not gonna forget that one.

00:35:07.458 --> 00:35:11.250
I can't believe her.
- She's so retarded sometimes.

00:35:11.333 --> 00:35:16.083
Shouldn't her boyfriend be doing this?
He's so worthless.

00:35:20.750 --> 00:35:25.708
Coop. Where are your keys?
How are we gonna find her keys?

00:35:28.083 --> 00:35:30.083
I can't find her keys.

00:35:30.083 --> 00:35:31.958
We can't wake her parents.
Her dad will go ballistic.

00:35:32.417 --> 00:35:34.417
I know.

00:35:35.375 --> 00:35:37.375
Bye, Coop.

00:35:38.958 --> 00:35:40.958
Call us.

00:35:58.792 --> 00:36:00.792
Hey.

00:36:02.083 --> 00:36:04.083
Get your keys.

00:37:26.250 --> 00:37:28.208
Thank God.

00:37:32.667 --> 00:37:36.167
What happened to your face?
- I got into a fight.

00:37:36.292 --> 00:37:41.042
With who? Why?
- I don't really know. I don't remember.

00:37:41.208 --> 00:37:44.667
I was really drunk.
I think I still am a little bit.

00:37:44.750 --> 00:37:47.792
Let's go. House. Now.

00:37:56.042 --> 00:37:59.625
You should have seen the waves coming
in. Six foot, and it was going off.

00:37:59.750 --> 00:38:02.167
Seth got into a fight.
- He did?

00:38:02.292 --> 00:38:06.375
This is what happens when you let
our son hang out with criminals.

00:38:06.458 --> 00:38:11.250
At least he has someone to hang out
with. Don't salt his game, honey.

00:38:11.333 --> 00:38:15.625
What the hell does that mean?
- It... I don't know.

00:38:15.792 --> 00:38:18.458
I just know I'd rather have Seth
hanging out with Ryan...

00:38:18.542 --> 00:38:19.958
...than some trust-fund kid...

00:38:20.042 --> 00:38:22.625
...who only cares about getting
a new Beemer every year.

00:38:22.750 --> 00:38:26.083
There's a whole world outside
this Newport Beach bubble.

00:38:26.208 --> 00:38:28.292
You don't seem to mind
living in this bubble.

00:38:28.417 --> 00:38:31.792
I know there's something else out there.

00:38:31.958 --> 00:38:33.917
Remember when we were 22?
What'd you say?

00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:37.167
That you'd never be like your parents,
you'd never have their life.

00:38:37.250 --> 00:38:41.458
I was 22. I stank of patchouli
and lived in the back of a mail truck.

00:38:41.542 --> 00:38:43.667
And you were fun.

00:38:43.875 --> 00:38:46.208
And rebellious and...

00:38:47.458 --> 00:38:49.542
You married me.

00:38:52.375 --> 00:38:55.458
I can't. I'm sorry.

00:38:57.958 --> 00:39:01.542
I don't want this kid in my house anymore.

00:39:03.000 --> 00:39:05.417
Where's he supposed to go?

00:39:05.583 --> 00:39:08.208
He has a family, Sandy.

00:39:08.375 --> 00:39:13.708
It's not up to you to decide
whether or not they're good enough.

00:39:22.042 --> 00:39:27.167
Look, Ryan, I don't mean to play bad cop.
It's nothing personal.

00:39:27.250 --> 00:39:29.250
Is that bacon?

00:39:31.458 --> 00:39:34.542
I usually make breakfast at my house.

00:39:34.833 --> 00:39:37.708
My mom's not much of a cook, so...

00:39:38.167 --> 00:39:42.833
I'm sorry. You seem like a really nice kid.
- It's okay.

00:39:43.250 --> 00:39:45.250
I get it.

00:39:52.208 --> 00:39:54.792
You have a really nice family.

00:40:21.667 --> 00:40:23.667
Hey, man.

00:40:26.333 --> 00:40:30.292
Hey.
- Hi. So I gotta jet.

00:40:31.750 --> 00:40:33.750
You're leaving?

00:40:35.333 --> 00:40:37.333
So...

00:40:39.750 --> 00:40:41.750
So, what's up?

00:40:41.875 --> 00:40:45.833
I gotta go back, try to figure
some stuff out back home.

00:40:45.958 --> 00:40:47.958
Okay, well...

00:40:48.583 --> 00:40:50.583
Cool.

00:40:51.708 --> 00:40:55.583
Not cool, but,
you know what I think I mean.

00:40:57.750 --> 00:40:59.750
Come here.

00:41:03.917 --> 00:41:08.750
I'll come down to Chino. I'll visit you,
and you can show me your world...

00:41:08.875 --> 00:41:11.417
...or, you know, ''hood' or...

00:41:11.958 --> 00:41:14.042
All right.

00:41:14.208 --> 00:41:17.250
Wait a second. Just wait one second.

00:41:24.708 --> 00:41:28.292
Maybe there's someplace you'll want to go.

00:41:28.917 --> 00:41:31.208
It's pretty good for ideas.

00:41:38.875 --> 00:41:40.875
Okay.

00:42:50.125 --> 00:42:52.583
So thanks...

00:42:52.750 --> 00:42:54.292
...for everything.

00:42:54.375 --> 00:42:58.292
I'm gonna make sure
everything works out, Ryan.

00:43:01.667 --> 00:43:04.625
It's okay. I can take it from here.

00:44:08.042 --> 00:44:10.625
Come on. Let's go.
